From: zigzag go-port/rustcore
Subject: [PATCH 5] feat(client): Client::forget_room_locally — the local half of Room::forget

Room::forget sends /forget, rewrites m.direct when the room was a DM, then
drops the room from the local stores (BaseClient::forget_room, crate-private).
zigzag forgets over plain HTTP, because that m.direct rewrite starts from
rust-sdk's own copy of m.direct and must not run. Without a way to the local
half, every room the app forgot stayed in the state store and the event cache
store for good.

- Client::forget_room_locally(room_id): BaseClient::forget_room as it is — the
  state store, the room held in memory, and the event cache store. Sends
  nothing.
- Client::forget_room_locally_if(room_id, states) /
  BaseClient::forget_room_if: the same, only while the room's state is one of
  `states`, checked and dropped from the state store under the state store
  lock that sync responses are processed under — so a sweep of rooms that
  looked left never drops one a response rejoined meanwhile. The event cache
  store is cleared after that lock is released (the event cache saves room
  info under it while holding its own lock). Returns whether it dropped it.

Upstreamable (generic, no app names).
---
diff --git a/crates/matrix-sdk-base/src/client.rs b/crates/matrix-sdk-base/src/client.rs
index c6a326c4f..d59e9246d 100644
--- a/crates/matrix-sdk-base/src/client.rs
+++ b/crates/matrix-sdk-base/src/client.rs
@@ -1066,6 +1066,32 @@ impl BaseClient {
         Ok(())
     }
 
+    /// [`Self::forget_room`], only while the room's state is one of `states`.
+    ///
+    /// The state is checked, and the room dropped from the state store, under
+    /// the state store lock that sync responses are processed under: a room a
+    /// response rejoined in between is kept. The event cache store is cleared
+    /// after the lock is released (the event cache saves room info under that
+    /// lock while it holds its own). Returns whether the room was dropped.
+    pub async fn forget_room_if(&self, room_id: &RoomId, states: &[RoomState]) -> Result<bool> {
+        {
+            let state_store_guard = self.state_store_lock().lock().await;
+            match self.state_store.room(room_id) {
+                Some(room) if states.contains(&room.state()) => {}
+                _ => return Ok(false),
+            }
+            self.state_store.forget_room_with_guard(&state_store_guard, room_id).await?;
+        }
+
+        match self.event_cache_store().lock().await? {
+            EventCacheStoreLockState::Clean(guard) | EventCacheStoreLockState::Dirty(guard) => {
+                guard.remove_room(room_id).await?
+            }
+        }
+
+        Ok(true)
+    }
+
